    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d137">

                <pb facs="0323" n="291" xml:id="pg291"/>

                <head>137. Memorandum of a Telephone Conversation Between the Secretary of State and the Deputy Assistant Secretary of State for
                    Far Eastern Affairs (Sebald),
                    Washington, April 26, 1955, 6:57 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d137-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1955-04-26T18:57:00-04:00"
                            >April 26, 1955, 6:57 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline></opener>
                <p>The Sec. asked if we have this paper re what we are going to do in Vietnam. S
                    said they have a 2nd draft.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d137-f2"/> The Sec. said he
                    does not want to see it now—but just wondered—it looks as though things are
                    getting critical fast and don’t know how much time we have. S. said they have it
                    worked out—just a question of tactics—how we make the approach. The Sec. said
                    let’s try to get something worked out as soon as possible. S. said they would
                    like to get to the Sec. as early as possible in the a.m.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
